<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n50568" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vermĭna</span></b> , um, n.
		vermis, gripings of the belly caused by worms; hence, in
		gen., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the
				gripes</i>, <i>belly-ache</i>, <i>stomach-ache.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">saeva,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Lucr.
					5, 997</span></i>
			; cf.: vermina dicuntur dolores corporis cum quodam minuto
			motu quasi a vermibus scindatur. Hic dolor Graece <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στρόφος</span> dicitur, <i><span class="en">Fest. p.
				375</span></i> Müll. —* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">passionum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Arn. 1, p. 30</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
